{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011iUXHrQiv1k7we2Q66djDz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"number\": 509,\n  \"title\": \"[BUG] Progress with transient=True leaves a blank line in Jupyter\",\n  \"body\": \"- [x] I've checked docs and closed issues for possible solutions.\\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the FAQ.\\n\\n**Describe the bug**\\n\\nIn a Jupyter notebook cell, a `Progress` with `transient=True` disappears when it finishes, but leaves an empty line above the next output.\\n\\n```python\\nfrom time import sleep\\nfrom rich.progress import Progress\\n\\nwith Progress(transient=True) as progress:\\n    task = progress.add_task(\\\"Working\\\", total=3)\\n    for _ in range(3):\\n        sleep(0.1)\\n        progress.advance(task)\\nprint(\\\"done\\\")\\n```\\n\\nIn a terminal only `done` is printed. In the notebook there is a blank line before `done`.\\n\\n**Platform**\\nJupyterLab 4.4, Python 3.12, Rich 14.3.3\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-30T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"Needs triage\"\n  ]\n}\ntotal 44\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 runner runner 4096 Oct 26 05:44 .\ndr-xr-xr-x 3 runner runner 4096 Oct 26 05:44 ..\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2404 Oct 26 05:44 _common.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2091 Oct 26 05:44 check_api.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 9041 Oct 26 05:44 check_comment.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 3476 Oct 26 05:44 check_report.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 1916 Oct 26 05:44 faq_match.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2618 Oct 26 05:44 find_duplicates.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 1641 Oct 26 05:44 validate_labels.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0d2d3a2-1722-400f-ae3a-10b590bdccc1","uuid":"024f0bbe-43c8-4174-b89c-ddad6b558e5d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:45:44.641Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"number\": 509,\n  \"title\": \"[BUG] Progress with transient=True leaves a blank line in Jupyter\",\n  \"body\": \"- [x] I've checked docs and closed issues for possible solutions.\\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the FAQ.\\n\\n**Describe the bug**\\n\\nIn a Jupyter notebook cell, a `Progress` with `transient=True` disappears when it finishes, but leaves an empty line above the next output.\\n\\n```python\\nfrom time import sleep\\nfrom rich.progress import Progress\\n\\nwith Progress(transient=True) as progress:\\n    task = progress.add_task(\\\"Working\\\", total=3)\\n    for _ in range(3):\\n        sleep(0.1)\\n        progress.advance(task)\\nprint(\\\"done\\\")\\n```\\n\\nIn a terminal only `done` is printed. In the notebook there is a blank line before `done`.\\n\\n**Platform**\\nJupyterLab 4.4, Python 3.12, Rich 14.3.3\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-30T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"Needs triage\"\n  ]\n}\ntotal 44\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 runner runner 4096 Oct 26 05:44 .\ndr-xr-xr-x 3 runner runner 4096 Oct 26 05:44 ..\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2404 Oct 26 05:44 _common.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2091 Oct 26 05:44 check_api.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 9041 Oct 26 05:44 check_comment.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 3476 Oct 26 05:44 check_report.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 1916 Oct 26 05:44 faq_match.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 2618 Oct 26 05:44 find_duplicates.py\n-r--r--r-- 1 runner runner 1641 Oct 26 05:44 validate_labels.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011iUXHrQiv1k7we2Q66djDz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
